Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 11:42:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(compliance): fix six real bugs found in a full Phase 1
 review
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Found via a fresh-database bootstrap, full test suite run, and an
independent code audit after the compliance-engine overhaul (43a8438):

- server/db.js: schema init crashed on a fresh database — the seed's
  UPDATE of clinical_service_orders.order_id ran before the ALTER TABLE
  that added the column. Moved the ALTER TABLE earlier, next to the
  table's other early column additions.
- server/db.js: pre_authorizations was missing a plan_name column that
  server.js already inserts into and selects from on every pre-auth
  request — GET/POST /api/preauth-requests were failing outright with
  "column plan_name does not exist". Added the column.
- server/db.js: the INV-93402 seed fixture linked its "Lipid Profile
  Panels" clinical order to master_service_id 2, which is actually
  "Erythrocyte Sedimentation Rate (ESR)" — an unrelated service with no
  catalogue entry, so the fixture surfaced as tariff_unknown instead of
  the intended price_mismatch. Corrected to master_service_id 8, which
  is the real Lipid Profile Panel entry.
- server.js: GET /api/compliance/summary crashed on invoice.created_at
  (a JS Date object from pg, not a string) — .split('T') isn't a Date
  method. Fixed by converting through new Date(...).toISOString() first.
- server.js: /api/compliance/summary's constituentOrders was always []
  in live-DB mode — invoices come from `SELECT * FROM invoices`, which
  has no joined `orders` field, so the field that reads invoice.orders
  never had anything to read. Now fetches and attaches each invoice's
  clinical_service_orders before building the summary.
- server.js: POST /api/compliance/invoices/:invoiceNumber/resolve
  returned raw `RETURNING *` (snake_case) in live-DB mode while the
  in-memory fallback returned camelCase — resolution.resolvedBy was
  undefined in production. Aliased the RETURNING columns.
- server.js: two duplicate-charge detection bugs in POST /api/invoices
  and computeInvoiceAuditFlags(). (1) The client-supplied orderId was
  used as the clinical_service_orders row's own primary key, so two
  line items sharing one orderId collided on INSERT ... ON CONFLICT
  (id) DO NOTHING and only one row was ever created — duplicate
  detection had nothing to compare against. (2) order_id wasn't even
  in the INSERT's column list, so it was never persisted regardless.
  Fixed the primary key to always be unique per line item, added
  order_id to the INSERT, and added a same-service-within-one-invoice
  duplicate check as a second detection layer for line items billed
  twice without an explicit shared orderId at all (this case was
  previously undetected outright, seed fixtures aside).

Verified against a fresh local Postgres database: tsc --noEmit and a
full production vite build both clean; every test suite now passes —
test_directory_catalogue (30), test_cost_estimation (20),
test_benefit_gaps, test_bill_audit (all, incl. one assertion updated
for the current duplicate-charge flag shape), test_compliance_summary
(all), test_preauth_overhaul (29), test_dva_transfer, test_dva_per_invoice.

